Local AI Agent & Support Ticket RAG

A local LLM project powered by LangChain, Ollama, and Chroma DB. This project demonstrates two core capabilities for local data processing:

Data Analysis Assistant (main.py): Prompts a local Llama model (llama3.2) to inspect, query, and analyze messy CSV datasets.

Support Ticket Vector Store (vectorbase.py): Uses local embeddings (mxbai-embed-large) to ingest and index customer support tickets into a Chroma vector database for semantic retrieval.

📁 Project Structure

.
├── main.py              # Interactive CLI session with Ollama Llama 3.2
├── vectorbase.py        # Vector database setup & document indexing via Chroma DB
├── support_tickets.csv  # Sample dataset containing support ticket records
├── requirements.txt     # Python dependencies
└── README.md            # Project documentation


🚀 Getting Started

1. Prerequisites

Make sure you have Ollama installed and running on your system.

Pull the required local models:

# Pull the LLM model
ollama pull llama3.2

# Pull the embedding model
ollama pull mxbai-embed-large


2. Installation

Clone or download this repository.

Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt


Dependencies included in requirements.txt:

langchain

langchain-ollama

langchain-chroma

pandas (required for CSV data processing)

🛠️ Usage

Running the Data Assistant (main.py)

Launch an interactive prompt session with the local LLM designed to analyze structured/unstructured dataset contexts safely:

python main.py


Features: Uses prompt engineering guidelines to handle messy datasets (inconsistent casing, extra spaces, missing values, date format variances) and prevents hallucination.

Building the Vector Database (vectorbase.py)

To build the Chroma vector store from support_tickets.csv:

python vectorbase.py


Features: Loads ticket data from support_tickets.csv, generates embeddings using mxbai-embed-large, and persists them locally under ./chromea_langchain_db.

📝 Configuration & Notes

Data Path: Ensure the file path to support_tickets.csv in vectorbase.py matches your local setup.

Database Directory: The persistent database will be automatically created at ./chromea_langchain_db upon first execution.
